WEBVTT

1
00:00:10.398 --> 00:00:16.262
the house felt empty and dismal after Mother left, the girls did their best to remain positive and

2
00:00:16.442 --> 00:00:19.564
optimistic about matters, at least most of the time.

3
00:00:19.584 --> 00:00:26.369
"If Aunt March makes one nasty remark to me today, I won't tolerate it," Jo grumbled as her

4
00:00:26.409 --> 00:00:32.417
hand automatically reached back to pull her long hair into a bun; when she remembered it wasn't there

5
00:00:32.477 --> 00:00:34.678
any more, she tugged at her short ends.

6
00:00:34.698 --> 00:00:41.782
"Jo, you must be on your best behavior today since Aunt March may be willing to help Father

7
00:00:42.242 --> 00:00:43.463
Meg remarked doubtfully.

8
00:00:43.483 --> 00:00:50.366
"Aunt March never has and never will help our family until the day she dies," Jo snorted unkindly.

9
00:00:50.386 --> 00:00:52.267
"Until who dies?"

10
00:00:52.668 --> 00:00:57.910
Beth inquired, walking toward her sisters with something steaming wrapped inside a kitchen towel.

11
00:00:59.291 --> 00:01:02.285
Meg glanced sharply at Jo, "Never mind, Beth.

12
00:01:02.845 --> 00:01:03.825
What have you got there?"

13
00:01:03.845 --> 00:01:11.449
"I thought you might need these," Beth said shyly, as she unwrapped two round (and slightly burnt) buns.

14
00:01:11.469 --> 00:01:16.631
"I baked them with old flour as Mother does, but they're not as nice as hers."

15
00:01:18.092 --> 00:01:22.994
Not only did the buns warm their hands, but Beth's kindness warmed their hearts even more.

16
00:01:23.014 --> 00:01:27.296
"Thank you, darling," said Meg, gently hugging her close.

17
00:01:28.416 --> 00:01:33.320
Meg and Jo left the house and as they were about to turn the corner, they looked back

18
00:01:33.801 --> 00:01:34.721
as they always did.

19
00:01:35.522 --> 00:01:40.546
This time, instead of Mother, Beth stood at the window waving at her sisters.

20
00:01:40.566 --> 00:01:47.271
"Sweet girl didn't forget," Jo said, wiping a tear from her eye.

21
00:01:48.192 --> 00:01:53.116
With lighter hearts and steps, the two March sisters proceeded to make their way to work.

22
00:01:54.068 --> 00:01:59.230
The March sisters promised Mother they would write as often as possible to keep her up-to-date on their

23
00:01:59.270 --> 00:01:59.970
lives at home.

24
00:02:00.930 --> 00:02:04.992
For Meg, the best time for her to collect her thoughts was after dinner.

25
00:02:06.152 --> 00:02:11.854
My Dearest Mother, How happy we were to receive your last letter and to find it containing such

26
00:02:11.934 --> 00:02:18.036
good news that even Laurie shed a tear or two, though he insists something went into his eye.

27
00:02:18.836 --> 00:02:23.938
We are so pleased that Father is recovering from his illness with your support and nursing skills to

28
00:02:23.998 --> 00:02:24.438
help him.

29
00:02:25.319 --> 00:02:26.659
Please send our love to him.

30
00:02:27.740 --> 00:02:33.502
The girls are behaving beautifully and cooperating with us so that everything is in order and well taken

31
00:02:33.562 --> 00:02:34.003
care of.

32
00:02:34.983 --> 00:02:40.485
Last night Amy decided she wanted to join the army when she was old enough but this morning

33
00:02:40.565 --> 00:02:45.087
she changed her mind and said she would be a better help for the community as a teacher

34
00:02:45.167 --> 00:02:46.568
or instructor of some sort.

35
00:02:47.604 --> 00:02:54.066
Jo unkindly laughed and the two of them exchanged heated words but they made up immediately and are

36
00:02:54.126 --> 00:02:55.506
now back to being friends.

37
00:02:56.787 --> 00:03:02.428
Beth hasn't been practicing the piano as often or as regularly because she feels that more important matters

38
00:03:02.488 --> 00:03:07.750
need her attention and it would be disloyal of her to do what she wants when everyone else

39
00:03:07.830 --> 00:03:09.670
is making personal sacrifices.

40
00:03:11.051 --> 00:03:15.772
We told her that you and Father both would want her to spend time for herself, but Beth

41
00:03:15.832 --> 00:03:21.015
feels that as long as you are away she must take on extra duties to make sure everything

42
00:03:21.075 --> 00:03:21.675
runs right.

43
00:03:22.875 --> 00:03:25.376
Dearest Mother, we are so grateful to Mr.

44
00:03:25.417 --> 00:03:28.398
Brookes, who has been a great strength to you during this time.

45
00:03:29.698 --> 00:03:34.761
Please extend our greetings and best wishes to him as well and tell him that we are eternally

46
00:03:34.821 --> 00:03:35.461
in his debt.

47
00:03:36.361 --> 00:03:39.383
We love you very much and anxiously await your return.

48
00:03:40.443 --> 00:03:47.995
Your loving daughter, Meg Since Jo was accustomed to waking early to write, she used that time to

49
00:03:48.035 --> 00:03:49.876
compose letters to Mother instead.

50
00:03:51.197 --> 00:03:57.061
To My Precious Mother, I always knew Father was a brave fighter and each day he will grow

51
00:03:57.121 --> 00:03:59.523
stronger and healthier with your support and love.

52
00:04:00.503 --> 00:04:05.747
We are very lonely without you, Mother, but I must say, the girls have been perfect angels.

53
00:04:07.028 --> 00:04:12.271
Meg watches over us like a mother hen (that's her new nickname, though I don't think she cares

54
00:04:12.331 --> 00:04:17.530
for it much), so Beth, Amy, and I, like meek chicks, obey her every word.

55
00:04:18.771 --> 00:04:25.335
Yesterday I nearly ended my friendship with Laurie because basically he called me a liar (though he didn't

56
00:04:25.495 --> 00:04:28.276
use those words exactly, it was what he implied).

57
00:04:29.037 --> 00:04:33.199
He said I agreed to go somewhere with him and I told him I did no such thing.

58
00:04:33.959 --> 00:04:37.621
Then we said some harsh words to each other and stomped off angrily.

59
00:04:38.402 --> 00:04:43.768
Then I remembered what you said about controlling my temper and I felt bad so I decided to

60
00:04:43.828 --> 00:04:47.069
apologize to Laurie, even though I still think I am right.

61
00:04:47.790 --> 00:04:51.891
But there he was, standing in front of our door, looking like a lost puppy.

62
00:04:52.791 --> 00:04:56.052
We both said sorry and are now best friends once again.

63
00:04:56.792 --> 00:05:00.233
I'm getting accustomed to my new hair and others seem to be as well.

64
00:05:01.033 --> 00:05:02.114
I even heard old Mrs.

65
00:05:02.154 --> 00:05:06.255
Kemper say that the boyish cut suits me and I took it as a compliment.

66
00:05:07.115 --> 00:05:09.016
Give my love to Father and greetings to Mr.

67
00:05:10.284 --> 00:05:13.085
Brookes. All my love to you, Mother, until I write again.

68
00:05:13.845 --> 00:05:22.047
Yours forever, Jo The two younger sisters wrote their letters whenever they felt like it, so theirs were

69
00:05:22.087 --> 00:05:24.588
shorter and more frequent than Meg's and Jo's.

70
00:05:25.608 --> 00:05:31.630
Dear Mother, I am sending some pressed pansies from the garden, as I am hoping that it will

71
00:05:31.650 --> 00:05:32.790
remind Father of home.

72
00:05:33.850 --> 00:05:38.572
I have also included a short note from the Hummels, though I wrote down what Mrs.

73
00:05:38.612 --> 00:05:41.294
Hummel said since her English is still quite poor.

74
00:05:42.295 --> 00:05:43.876
The children all seem to be well.

75
00:05:44.597 --> 00:05:46.518
They miss you almost as much as I do.

76
00:05:47.339 --> 00:05:49.341
Please give Father a kiss from his Beth.

77
00:05:50.061 --> 00:05:51.262
I love you, Mother dearest.

78
00:05:51.943 --> 00:05:59.790
Little Beth My Loving Mother, You will be happy to know that I am doing my lessons faithfully.

79
00:06:00.691 --> 00:06:06.155
Jo was so cross with me the other day because I forgot (I really did) to write my

80
00:06:06.295 --> 00:06:10.114
essay. But today she seemed pleased with what I showed her.

81
00:06:10.914 --> 00:06:12.275
I'm back with oils now.

82
00:06:12.616 --> 00:06:17.459
I find that clay doesn't allow me to express my emotions as clearly as oils do.

83
00:06:18.800 --> 00:06:21.722
I've inserted a picture I completed just this morning.

84
00:06:22.703 --> 00:06:25.084
Please tell Father it is drawn with love.

85
00:06:26.105 --> 00:06:28.507
I am thinking about cutting my hair like Jo's.

86
00:06:29.447 --> 00:06:33.930
I rather like that carefree style and feel that it would go well with my natural curls.

87
00:06:34.791 --> 00:06:35.852
What do you think, Mother?

88
00:06:37.128 --> 00:06:42.130
Mr. Laurence visits us daily and every other day we are invited to dine at the mansion.

89
00:06:43.111 --> 00:06:49.333
His cook has excellent taste and prepares for us cuisine from the continent (which is Europe, in case

90
00:06:49.373 --> 00:06:50.073
you didn't know).

91
00:06:51.094 --> 00:06:54.015
Just the other day she prepared a French meal for us.

92
00:06:54.755 --> 00:06:56.416
Mother, it was heaven.

93
00:06:57.436 --> 00:06:59.857
One day I must go over and learn her art.

94
00:07:01.338 --> 00:07:03.179
Oh, it sounds like Jo is back home.

95
00:07:03.799 --> 00:07:08.821
I'd better get back to my lessons or else Please give my love to Father.

96
00:07:09.421 --> 00:07:15.845
Affectionately, Amy Whenever or wherever the girls wrote their letters was up to them.

97
00:07:16.765 --> 00:07:23.269
When they received a letter from Mother, however, the sisters gathered closely together to listen and find comfort

98
00:07:23.309 --> 00:07:29.012
in Mother's loving words, which helped them to have hope, joy, and faith for the future.
